\code{goseq} package keeps them, which enlarges the BH denominator and makes it
more conservative (set \code{drop_empty_cats = FALSE} to match \code{goseq} instead).

The returned tibble carries \code{\link[=run_ora]{run_ora()}}'s columns, in \code{\link[=run_ora]{run_ora()}}'s order,
so it is a drop-in for downstream code. goseq-specific columns
(\code{p_uncorrected}, \code{odds}, \code{method}) are appended at the end.
